Falsifies `jh7110_clock_and_reset::verification::with_parent_changes_only_the_mux_field`.

The defect: the parent is shifted into place but no longer cut to the four-bit field, so a parent
wider than four bits spills into the divider and the enable bit. A clock that was gated comes up
running mid-switch, which the function exists to prevent.

Expected to fail: the harness's assertion that every bit outside `CLOCK_PARENT_MASK` is unchanged.

diff --git a/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs b/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
index 7cc680a83..333afdc34 100644
--- a/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/jh7110_clock_and_reset/src/lib.rs
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@ pub(crate) const CLOCK_MUX_SHIFT: u32 = 24;
 /// Name: ratified 2026-10-26 (UTC).
 #[must_use]
 pub const fn with_parent(word: u32, parent: u32) -> u32 {
-    (word & !CLOCK_PARENT_MASK) | ((parent << CLOCK_MUX_SHIFT) & CLOCK_PARENT_MASK)
+    (word & !CLOCK_PARENT_MASK) | (parent << CLOCK_MUX_SHIFT)
 }
 
